# Everything generated as you study. Personal to this clone — not the repository.
# Keeps the kit a clean template you can `git pull` into without conflicts.
#
# All of it is written by the /teach and /quiz tutor flows (see CLAUDE.md,
# "Study output is personal, not repository"). Never commit these, and never
# remove them from this file — one learner's progress is not the kit.

# Why you're learning this — written once by /teach at session 1, then evolves.
MISSION.md

# The tutor's scratchpad: learner profile, depth defaults, session log.
NOTES.md

# Progress tracker, if your tooling writes one; same policy as the rest.
PROGRESS.md

# One self-contained HTML file per completed lesson unit (30 of the 47 units).
# The resume rule reads this directory: lowest-numbered unit with no file is next.
lessons/

# Numbered insight records (like ADRs for learning) — misses, corrections,
# and carry-ins for future units, logged by task statement number.
learning-records/

# Cheat sheets, decision cards and the glossary — the compressed, revisitable
# essence of the lessons.
reference/

# Shared components every lesson links: course.css, quiz.js, match.js.
assets/

# Practice quizzes and mock exams generated by the /quiz skill.
practice/

# Design specs and plans written by agent workflows (e.g. superpowers) while
# working on this clone's local tooling.
docs/
